  'keyword.title':       'Keyword Monitoring',
  'keyword.subtitle':    'Monitor the presence/absence of a keyword in web pages (case-insensitive).',
  'keyword.how1': 'A direct GET from the monitoring server (single pod); redirects are followed and SSL verification is OFF (internal-CA/self-signed pages work too — certificate validity is a separate monitor type). The body is read but capped at ~2 MB (memory guard). 443 is not required; the scheme depends on the monitor URL. The egress path follows the form\'s “Corporate proxy” setting (Same as inventory = the certificate-inventory record; Always via proxy / Direct) — same proxy and NO_PROXY rule as certificate checks.',
  'keyword.how2': 'The keyword is searched in the body; case-insensitive by default (case-sensitive via a toggle). The present/absent condition and count threshold (≥, ≤, =, >, <) are applied by the scheduler. Result: found or not, count, status code, response time, short snippet.',
